From 4875af22a155c379347102e9a17db91c2112436b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: primez <mpincoski@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 07:52:33 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 34/41] [TSReader] Keep E-AC-3 access units whole across
 segments, and drop released audio at a seek

Round 10 findings (Astra):

- An E-AC-3 access unit whose PES continues in the next segment after
  the first bytes of the dependent header came out as two samples. The
  parser now waits while the bytes after a frame are too few to tell a
  dependent header (DependentFrameSize returns -1). At the end of the
  data, the parser waits for the rest of a started dependent frame, and
  sends a frame alone only when no bytes follow.
- A dependent header with a frame size below the AC-3 header or the
  reserved sample rate codes joined data that is no frame. The header
  checks now match FindHeaders().
- The packet that ReadEndPacket returns at a segment end did not update
  the segment anchor of the audio frame. ReadPacket and ReadEndPacket
  now share PacketRead.
- Held audio that ReleaseUntimed moved to m_samples before a seek came
  out after the seek. TimeSeek now clears m_samples.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
